---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  icon="shield"
  compact
  section="Page"
  title="Privacy"
  kicker="Legal"
  description="What this site collects, why, and how to opt out — the contact form and third-party services."
  wide={false}
  imageAlt="Noah Weidig's privacy policy"
>
  <div class="prose-nw">
    <p class="text-faint">
      <em>Last updated: 28 July 2026</em>
    </p>

    <p>
      This is a personal portfolio site. It sells nothing, has no accounts, and collects as little
      as it can get away with.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The site runs no analytics or tracking scripts, sets no cookies, and stores nothing in your
      browser between visits. I do not know who reads it or how often.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> is handled by{' '}
      <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy">Formspree</a>. Whatever you type into it —
      your name, email address, and message — is transmitted to Formspree and forwarded to my inbox.
      It is used to reply to you and nothing else: no mailing list, no sharing, no resale. You can
      email me directly at <a href="mailto:noah@noahweidig.com">noah@noahweidig.com</a> instead if
      you would rather skip the intermediary.
    </p>

    <h2>Scheduling</h2>
    <p>
      The "Book a Call" links go to <a href="https://cal.com/privacy">Cal.com</a>, which handles its
      own booking data under its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and fonts</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static, served by GitHub Pages, with deploy previews on Netlify. Both keep
      standard server request logs, which I do not have access to. Fonts are self-hosted, so no font
      CDN sees your visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      If you are in the EU, UK, or another jurisdiction with data protection law and want to know
      what I hold about you, or want it deleted, email{' '}
      <a href="mailto:noah@noahweidig.com">noah@noahweidig.com</a>. In practice the only thing that
      ever exists is a message you sent me yourself.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
